# ── Shipped sample data ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# test_data/ ships with the repo so the GUI works out of the box. Re-include its
# data files despite the global *.tif/*.h5/... ignores above (order matters — these
# negations come last). Generated outputs and scratch files stay ignored.
!test_data/**/*.tif
!test_data/**/*.tiff
!test_data/**/*.h5
!test_data/**/*.hdf5
!test_data/**/*.json
!test_data/**/*.csv
!test_data/**/*.txt
!test_data/**/*.py
!test_data/**/*.png
test_data/output/
test_data/out_temp.txt
# Large local-only sample sets kept out of git (directory-level ignore overrides
# the *.tif/*.txt/... re-includes above; a whole ignored dir cannot be re-included).
/test_data/17BM/
/test_data/test_s25ide/
# PDF tab test data: 5 raw .vrx.h5 detector frames (~320 MB) + calibration +
# pre-integrated I(Q) — too large to ship in the repo; kept local-only like
# test_data_pump_probe/ below. tab_pdf.py's DEFAULT_PDF_* constants point
# here, so the PDF tab just won't have data preloaded on a fresh checkout.
/test_data/test_pdf/

# ── Pump Probe (TR-XRD) local test data ──────────────────────────────────────
# Large local-only asset (~1.2 GB of detector frames + masks + MIDAS param file)
# that the Pump Probe tab defaults to. Kept out of git entirely (unlike test_data/,
# which ships with the repo). The negations above only re-include test_data/**.
/test_data_pump_probe/

# Large local-only functional-test dataset (kept out of git entirely).
/test_data_gitignore/

# Internal-only documentation (kept local, not published to GitHub)
documentation/pdf_calculation_explained.md
documentation/pdf_calculation_explained.pdf
